      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that a “proximate explanation” is specifically an account in terms of “immediate underlying mechanisms.” The provided packet does not define proximate explanation in those terms; it only uses the phrase in connection with Peto’s paradox.",
        "The definition’s refinement—“identifying the exact molecular processes that promote tumor formation”—is only broadly echoed by the packet’s statement about “exact molecular mechanisms promoting the process of tumorigenesis,” but the definition adds more specific wording (“tumor formation”) than is directly supported by the packet.",
        "The packet supports that this approach “may provide a proximate explanation of Peto’s paradox,” but it does not supply the general conceptual definition that the first sentence asserts."
